{"dependencies":[],"dependents":[],"events":[{"description":"Emitted when start() has finished starting the node.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\": bool,\n\"message\": string\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageStart","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageStart(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when stop() has finished stopping the node.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\": bool,\n\"message\": string\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageStop","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageStop(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when connect() has finished connecting to the peer.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\": bool,\n\"message\": string\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageConnect","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageConnect(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted as uploadUrl() or uploadChunk() upload data.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\":   bool,\n\"sessionId\": string,\n\"bytes\":     number,       // present on success\n\"total\":     number,       // file size in bytes\n\"error\":     string        // present on failure\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageUploadProgress","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageUploadProgress(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when uploadUrl() finishes.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\":   bool,\n\"sessionId\": string,\n\"cid\":       string,       // present on success\n\"error\":     string        // present on failure\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageUploadDone","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageUploadDone(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted as downloadToUrl() or downloadChunks() receive data.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\":   true,\n\"sessionId\": string,\n\"bytes\":     number,       // file download (downloadToUrl)\n\"total\":     number,       // file download; dataset size in bytes\n\"chunk\":     string        // base64 chunk, stream download (downloadChunks)\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageDownloadProgress","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageDownloadProgress(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when downloadToUrl() or downloadChunks() finishes.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\":   bool,\n\"sessionId\": string,\n\"error\":     string        // present on failure\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageDownloadDone","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageDownloadDone(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when downloadManifest() finishes.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\": bool,\n\"cid\":     string,\n\"manifest\": {              // present on success\n\"manifestVersion\": number,\n\"treeCid\":     string,\n\"datasetSize\": number,\n\"blockSize\":   number,\n\"filename\":    string,\n\"mimetype\":    string\n},\n\"error\":   string          // present on failure\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageDownloadManifestDone","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageDownloadManifestDone(tstr)","type":"event"},{"description":"Emitted when remove() finishes.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"success\": bool,\n\"cid\":     string,\n\"error\":   string          // present on failure\n}\n@endcode","name":"storageRemoveDone","parameters":[{"name":"payload","type":"tstr"}],"signature":"storageRemoveDone(tstr)","type":"event"}],"methods":[{"description":"Migrate the configuration after a Storage Module update.\n\nThis method takes a configuration string in parameters and returns\na new configuration JSON string updated.\n\nDepending on the updates of logos-storage-nim, some options can be removed\nor replaced with new ones. This method ensures a migration path for the\nconfiguration to the latest version of the module using a configuration version.\n\nIn addition to the migration, the data-dir is also set if it is not provided\nin configuration. And with `mix-enabled` true plus a network key, the mix\nconfiguration is updated.\n\nThis method should be called before `init()`. It is a separate step so\nthe caller can get the result of the new configuration and update it.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as the JSON to hand to init().","isInvokable":true,"name":"migrateConfig","parameters":[{"name":"cfg","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"migrateConfig(tstr)"},{"description":"Create a new storage node instance and configure it.\n\n`cfg` is a JSON string with the configuration overwriting defaults.\n\nExample of JSON config:\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"log-level\": \"info\",\n\"log-format\": \"auto\",\n\"metrics\": false,\n\"metrics-address\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n\"metrics-port\": 8008,\n\"data-dir\": \".cache/storage\",\n\"listen-ip\": \"0.0.0.0\",\n\"listen-port\": 0,\n\"nat\": \"auto\",\n\"net-privkey\": \"key\",\n\"bootstrap-node\": [],\n\"no-bootstrap-node\": false,\n\"network\": \"logos.test\",\n\"dht-mix-proxy\": [],\n\"mix-enabled\": false,\n\"mix-pool\": \"\",\n\"mix-pool-json\": \"\",\n\"max-peers\": 160,\n\"num-threads\": 0,\n\"agent-string\": \"Logos Storage\",\n\"repo-kind\": \"fs\",\n\"storage-quota\": 21474836480,\n\"block-ttl\": \"30d\",\n\"block-mi\": \"10m\",\n\"block-mn\": 1000,\n\"block-retries\": 300,\n\"log-file\": \"/tmp/storage-log-624036264.log\",\n\"nat-schedule-interval\": \"2m\",\n\"nat-num-peers-to-ask\": 3,\n\"nat-max-queue-size\": 3,\n\"nat-min-confidence\": 0.6,\n\"nat-observed-addr-min-count\": 1,\n\"nat-max-relays\": 2,\n\"nat-port-mapping-discover-timeout\": 500,\n\"nat-port-mapping-timeout\": 500,\n\"nat-port-mapping-recheck-period\": 300000\n}\n@endcode\n\nDo not call init() more than once per instance.\n\nReturns true on success.  The method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"init","parameters":[{"name":"cfg","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"bool","signature":"init(tstr)"},{"description":"Start the storage node.\n\nReturns true if the start command was accepted by libstorage.  Actual\ncompletion is signalled asynchronously via the `storageStart` event.\n\nThe method is asynchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"start","returnType":"bool","signature":"start()"},{"description":"Stop the storage node.\n\nThe node can be started and stopped multiple times.  Returns a\nStdLogosResult indicating whether the stop command was sent; actual\ncompletion is signalled via the `storageStop` event.\n\nThe method is asynchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"stop","returnType":"result","signature":"stop()"},{"description":"Destroy the storage context and free all resources.\n\nInternally calls storage_close then storage_destroy.  The node should\nbe stopped before calling destroy().  Not stopping first can lead to\nundefined behaviour (e.g. data loss or crashes).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::success = true on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"destroy","returnType":"result","signature":"destroy()"},{"description":"Get the libstorage version string.\n\nNamed for what it returns: this is the version of the underlying\nlibstorage (Nim) library, NOT of this module. `version()` cannot be used\nfor it -- that name is reserved for module identity and must be\n`version() -> tstr`, which the generator injects from `metadata.json`.\n\nDoes not require the node to be started.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a std::string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"libstorageVersion","returnType":"result","signature":"libstorageVersion()"},{"description":"Get this module's version, as declared in `metadata.json`.\n\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"moduleVersion","returnType":"tstr","signature":"moduleVersion()"},{"description":"Get the storage data directory path.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a std::string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"dataDir","returnType":"result","signature":"dataDir()"},{"description":"Get the Logos network this node was configured for.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a std::string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"network","returnType":"result","signature":"network()"},{"description":"Get the node's peer ID.\n\nThe peer ID is the libp2p peer identity as described at\nhttps://docs.libp2p.io/concepts/fundamentals/peers/\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a std::string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"peerId","returnType":"result","signature":"peerId()"},{"description":"Get the node's Signed Peer Record (SPR).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a std::string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"spr","returnType":"result","signature":"spr()"},{"description":"Get debug information for the node.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a JSON object on success:\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"id\": string,\n\"addrs\": [string],\n\"spr\": string,\n\"table\": {\n\"localNode\": { \"peerId\": string, \"addresses\": [string],\n\"lastSeen\": null },\n\"nodes\": [{ \"peerId\": string, \"addresses\": [string],\n\"lastSeen\": int }]\n}\n}\n@endcode\n\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"debug","returnType":"result","signature":"debug()"},{"description":"Collect node metrics for the openmetrics module.\n\nImplements the openmetrics-module IMetricsSource interface. Returns a\nLogos openmetrics-compatible JSON object. On libstorage errors or invalid\npayloads, returns: { \"metrics\": [] }.\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"metrics\": [\n{\n\"name\": string,\n\"type\": string,\n\"help\": string,\n\"value\": number,\n\"labels\": object\n}\n]\n}\n@endcode\n\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"collectMetrics","returnType":"{tstr: any}","signature":"collectMetrics()"},{"description":"Set the log level at runtime.\n\n`logLevel` must be one of: TRACE, DEBUG, INFO, NOTICE, WARN, ERROR, FATAL\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::success = true on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"updateLogLevel","parameters":[{"name":"logLevel","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"updateLogLevel(tstr)"},{"description":"Connect to a peer.\n\nUses `peerAddresses` as explicit dial targets when provided; otherwise\nthe peer must be discoverable via the DHT using `peerId`.\n\nReturns a StdLogosResult indicating whether the connect command was sent;\nactual completion is signalled via the `storageConnect` event.\n\nThe method is asynchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"connect","parameters":[{"name":"peerId","type":"tstr"},{"name":"peerAddresses","type":"[tstr]"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"connect(tstr,[tstr])"},{"description":"Toggle routing of DHT queries over the Logos mix network.\n\nWhen enabled, all subsequent DHT queries are tunnelled over Mix; this\naffects queries only, not advertisements.\n\nEnabling requires Mix to be configured: `mix-enabled` true and at\nleast one `dht-mix-proxy` set (see init()). Otherwise enabling fails\nwith an error. Disabling is always allowed.\n\nThis is a temporary API and will likely be removed before mainnet.\n\nOn success, returns StdLogosResult::value as a bool: the previous toggle\nstate (true = private queries were already enabled).\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"togglePrivateQueries","parameters":[{"name":"enabled","type":"bool"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"togglePrivateQueries(bool)"},{"description":"Upload a local file by absolute path.\n\nInternally calls storage_upload_init followed by storage_upload_file.\nIf init succeeds but the file upload command fails, the session is\ncancelled automatically.\n\n`filePath`  – absolute path to the file on disk.\n`chunkSize` – upload chunk size in bytes (default 65536).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a session ID string on success.\n\nThe method is asynchronous; progress is signalled via the\n`storageUploadProgress` event (throttled to at most one event per %\npoint) and completion via the `storageUploadDone` event.","isInvokable":true,"name":"uploadUrl","parameters":[{"name":"filePath","type":"tstr"},{"name":"chunkSize","type":"int"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"uploadUrl(tstr,int)"},{"description":"Create a manual upload session for chunk-by-chunk streaming.\n\nUse this only when uploadUrl() cannot be used (e.g. you are streaming\ndata that is not on disk).  After creating a session, send all chunks\nwith uploadChunk(), then call uploadFinalize() to get the CID.\n\n`filename`  – used to populate manifest metadata (mimetype, name).\n`chunkSize` – upload chunk size in bytes (default 65536).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as the session ID string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"uploadInit","parameters":[{"name":"filename","type":"tstr"},{"name":"chunkSize","type":"int"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"uploadInit(tstr,int)"},{"description":"Upload a single data chunk for a session created with uploadInit().\n\nA failed chunk does not corrupt the session; the caller may retry or\ncall uploadCancel().\n\nEmits the `storageUploadProgress` event on completion.\n\nThe method is asynchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"uploadChunk","parameters":[{"name":"sessionId","type":"tstr"},{"name":"chunk","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"uploadChunk(tstr,tstr)"},{"description":"Finalize a manual upload session and retrieve the CID.\n\nMust be called after all chunks have been sent with uploadChunk().\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as the CID string on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"uploadFinalize","parameters":[{"name":"sessionId","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"uploadFinalize(tstr)"},{"description":"Cancel an ongoing upload session.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::success = true on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"uploadCancel","parameters":[{"name":"sessionId","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"uploadCancel(tstr)"},{"description":"Download content by CID and write it to a local file.\n\nInternally fetches the manifest first to obtain the total size (required\nfor progress throttling); returns an error if the manifest is unavailable.\n\n`cid`       – content identifier to download.\n`filePath`  – destination path on disk.\n`local`     – if true, only reads from locally cached data (no network).\n`chunkSize` – download chunk size in bytes (default 65536).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as the session ID (= CID) on success.\n\nThe method is asynchronous; progress is signalled via the\n`storageDownloadProgress` event (throttled to at most one event per %\npoint) and completion via the `storageDownloadDone` event.","isInvokable":true,"name":"downloadToUrl","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"},{"name":"filePath","type":"tstr"},{"name":"local","type":"bool"},{"name":"chunkSize","type":"int"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"downloadToUrl(tstr,tstr,bool,int)"},{"description":"Download content by CID and deliver it as a stream of base64-encoded chunks.\n\nUse this when you want to process or forward the data without writing it\nto disk.  For large files, downloadToUrl() is more efficient as it avoids\nthe base64 encoding overhead.\n\n`cid`       – content identifier to download.\n`local`     – if true, only reads from locally cached data (no network).\n`chunkSize` – download chunk size in bytes (default 65536).\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as the session ID (= CID) on success.\n\nThe method is asynchronous; each chunk is delivered via the\n`storageDownloadProgress` event (one event per chunk, not throttled) and\ncompletion via the `storageDownloadDone` event.","isInvokable":true,"name":"downloadChunks","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"},{"name":"local","type":"bool"},{"name":"chunkSize","type":"int"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"downloadChunks(tstr,bool,int)"},{"description":"Cancel an ongoing download session.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::success = true on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"downloadCancel","parameters":[{"name":"sessionId","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"downloadCancel(tstr)"},{"description":"Check whether content identified by CID exists in local storage.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as bool (true = exists) on success.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"exists","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"exists(tstr)"},{"description":"Fetch content from the network and cache it locally in the background.\n\nThe method returns as soon as the fetch request is accepted; no event is\nemitted when the background download completes.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::success = true if the request was accepted.\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"fetch","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"fetch(tstr)"},{"description":"Remove content identified by CID from local storage in the background.\n\nThe delete may touch the network and can take a while, so this method\ndoes not block: the returned StdLogosResult only reports whether the\ncommand was dispatched. The real outcome arrives later via the\n`storageRemoveDone` event.","isInvokable":true,"name":"remove","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"remove(tstr)"},{"description":"Get storage space information.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a JSON object on success:\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"totalBlocks\":        number,\n\"quotaMaxBytes\":      number,\n\"quotaUsedBytes\":     number,\n\"quotaReservedBytes\": number\n}\n@endcode\n\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"space","returnType":"result","signature":"space()"},{"description":"List all manifests stored locally.\n\nReturns StdLogosResult::value as a JSON array on success; each item:\n@code{.json}\n{\n\"cid\":         string,\n\"treeCid\":     string,\n\"datasetSize\": number,\n\"blockSize\":   number,\n\"filename\":    string,\n\"mimetype\":    string\n}\n@endcode\n\nThe method is synchronous.","isInvokable":true,"name":"manifests","returnType":"result","signature":"manifests()"},{"description":"Fetch the manifest for a given CID in the background.\n\nThe lookup may query the DHT and can take a long time, so this method\ndoes not block: the returned StdLogosResult only reports whether the\ncommand was dispatched. The real outcome arrives later via the\n`storageDownloadManifestDone` event.","isInvokable":true,"name":"downloadManifest","parameters":[{"name":"cid","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"result","signature":"downloadManifest(tstr)"},{"description":"Import all files from a directory (headless helper).\n\nIterates regular files in `path` and calls uploadUrl() for each.\nDoes not wait for uploads to complete; listen for `storageUploadDone`\nevents to track results.","isInvokable":true,"name":"importFiles","parameters":[{"name":"path","type":"tstr"}],"returnType":"void","signature":"importFiles(tstr)"},{"description":"The module's name, as declared in its metadata.","isInvokable":true,"name":"name","returnType":"tstr","signature":"name()"},{"description":"The module's version, as declared in its metadata.","isInvokable":true,"name":"version","returnType":"tstr","signature":"version()"},{"description":"The module's canonical LIDL interface document.","isInvokable":true,"name":"lidl","returnType":"tstr","signature":"lidl()"}],"name":"storage_module","status":"loaded","uptime_seconds":0,"version":"2.1.3"}
